# Aspire architecture

Stack: TypeScript, Playwright Test, Node.js. Do not generate JavaScript test files.

Layers (top to bottom): tests → business flows → pages/components → core → Playwright.

- Tests express business intent only. No locators, no raw click/fill sequences, no env URLs or secrets.
- Flows own multi-step journeys and take explicit dependencies (pages, API clients).
- Pages encapsulate locators and page actions. Components own shared UI (header, table, modal, toast, pagination).
- Core stays thin (`BasePage`, env loader). Do not wrap Playwright without a real gap.
- Fixtures compose pages/flows and isolate browser context. Config switches environments without changing tests.

Do not create domain Page Objects or tests until the app URL and assignment behavior are known.

Search the repo before adding a page, flow, fixture, or util. Prefer composition over inheritance. Every new abstraction must solve a concrete duplication or isolation problem.

```typescript
// ✅ tests call flows
await candidateFlow.createCandidate(candidate);

// ❌ tests drive the DOM
await page.locator('#email').fill(email);
```
